icc_ra_t9363_side_ldr_mdr_township", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"side_boundary_setback\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"lot width <= 12.5 m: 0.9 m\", \"lot width > 12.5 m and < 15.0 m: 1 m (row text reads 'Not greater than 12.5 metres, but less than 15.0 metres')\", \"lot width >= 15.0 m and < 20 m: ground floor 1 m; second storey 1.5 m\", \"lot width >= 20.0 m: ground floor 1.2 m; second storey 2.0 m\", \"any width: third storey and above 2 m\"], \"exceptions\": [\"Note: the Queensland Development Code setbacks apply for dwelling houses and dual occupancies\"], \"formula_text\": null}\nLot conditions (not encoded): banded by width of lot\nStructure scope 'Buildings and other structures' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO - the table note defers dwelling houses to QDC setbacks; Class 10a building work is assessed against PO 22/PO 23 only (Table 5.7.1)\nResearcher notes: Band wording is literally 'Not greater than 12.5 metres, but less than 15.0 metres' and 'Not greater than 15.0 metres, but less than 20 metres' (drafting error; read as 'greater than'). AO 4.2 calls the table 'minimum road and boundary setbacks' but the table title is 'minimum side and rear boundary setbacks'. Because of the QDC note this table effectively applies to dwelling houses' outbuildings only if a curator decides the note does not reach Class 10 ancillary structures; default reading: QDC applies to dwelling houses and their Class 10a buildings."}$q$::jsonb);
